# adventure.adv -- THE HAND-EDITED game-data corpus (28-Aug-26, final
# source model after the owner archived the legacy loaders and their
# @NAME/@ROOM-format source files). advdataloader compiles this ONE file
# into every generated include (adv_msgtab.ah, adv_roomtab.ah,
# adv_drumlayout.ah, adv_objdefs.ah, the six adv_obj*.ac tables,
# adv_verbtab.ac) and loads the drum -- `make` in Adventure/ runs the
# chain.
#
# Sections, in order (grammar reference: this directory's README.md):
#   messages   -- `message NAME` ... text ... `@`; \n
#                 join with a space; '_' is reserved (newline sentinel)
#   movement / flags / actions -- named numeric values
#   rooms      -- room NAME / longmsg / shortmsg / flag / exit ... end;
#                 ROOM ORDER = room numbering. A new room may be inserted
#                 at ANY position in this section (not just appended) --
#                 doing so renumbers every room after the insertion point
#                 and invalidates existing drum saves (SAVE_ROOMVIS and
#                 objloc are both indexed by room number); this is
#                 accepted, no mitigation needed (owner decision 1,
#                 PendingRework/TASK-ROOM-FLAG-WORD.md). No game logic
#                 depends on room ORDER any more -- the last three
#                 positional room-region checks were replaced by the
#                 per-room SURFACE flag by that same task.
#   objects    -- object statements; ORDER = OBJ_* index order (append
#                 only, unless renumbering is intended); syntax in the
#                 section's own header comments below
#   verbs      -- verb NAME voc WORD (move DIR|none|msgref MSG|karg N)
#                 handler H; ORDER = verbTab match precedence; emitted
#                 as adv_verbtab.ac (TASK-VERB-EMISSION, live 29-Aug-26)
# Bare integers are OCTAL; 0d = decimal; 0x = hex (am1 conventions).
#
# History: originally generated by convert_legacy.py from the archived
# Text/adventureText.txt + Rooms/adventureRooms.txt (+ the pre-S2
# hand-coded object tables); that tool and this file's generated-era
# headers are historical as of today.

message GREETING
WELCOME TO ADVENTURE ON THE PDP-1!.\n
TYPE COMMANDS OF ONE OR TWO WORDS, SUCH AS LOOK, NORTH,\n
UP, DOWN, TAKE KEYS, ON, OFF, UNLOCK,
OPEN, XYZZY, INVENTORY, HELP, OR QUIT.\n
COMMANDS MAY BE TYPED IN UPPER OR LOWER CASE.\n
TYPE HELP AT ANY TIME FOR A FULL COMMAND LIST.
@
message FAREWELL
GOODBYE.\n
THANKS FOR PLAYING.
@
message ROAD_LONG
YOU ARE STANDING AT THE END OF A ROAD BEFORE A SMALL BRICK BUILDING.\n
AROUND YOU IS A FOREST.\n
A SMALL STREAM FLOWS OUT OF THE BUILDING AND DOWN A GULLY.
@
