# msgs TAKEN ("TAKEN.") and DROPPED ("DROPPED.") were removed here in
# TASK-FR28 N23, 05-Sep-26, for the same reason CANT_TAKE went in S16:
# they are strings adven.dat does not contain.  adven.f4 9014 ends a
# successful TAKE with "GOTO 2009", and 2009 is "K=54" -> 2010 "SPK=K"
# -> 2011 "CALL RSPEAK(SPK)"; a successful DROP falls through the four
# special legs to 9027, the ORDINARY path, which is "CALL RSPEAK(54)"
# before 9021's mechanics.  Message 54 is "OK".  (9021, which the FR28
# row cited, is the mechanics tail, and it is silent only because the
# legs that jump into it -- 9020's msg 30 and 9026's msg 163 -- have
# already spoken.)  dtgRepoDone and ddDoDrop now both print msg_OK, the
# record this file already carries and ulDoor's oiled leg already uses.
# Owner's ruling 04-Sep-26, recorded in FUNCTIONALITY.md's "Considered
# and NOT added" list: the Fortran is the final arbiter.  Do not re-add
# either record.
# msg CANT_TAKE ("YOU CAN'T TAKE THAT.") was removed here in S16,
# 04-Sep-26. It is a string adven.dat does not contain; adven.f4 9010
# refuses a TAKE with msg 25 / 115 / 169 / 170 and never with an
# invented one. S15's L10 fix rewired the last caller (dtCantTake ->
# msg_CANT_BE_SERIOUS / BEAR_CHAINED / CHAIN_LOCKED), leaving this
# record referenced by nothing. Owner's ruling 04-Sep-26: the Fortran
# is the arbiter, so it goes. Do not re-add it.
