# 19 311028 45 36 / 19 311029 46 37 / 19 311030 44 7
# TASK-FR4 LOC 19, S44 (06-Sep-26).  All six snake-gated words are here
# now.  NORTH's gate is NOT missing and never was: doMove's mtkSnakeCheck
# owns NORTH/SOUTH/WEST/SW while the snake is present and bounces them off
# FORCED LOC 32 (adventure.am1's mtkBounce), so those three never reach
# this table in that state.  FR2 step 4's note above this block said the
# opposite and mirrored LEFT on it -- an UNGATED row -- which let LEFT walk
# the player past the snake to LOC 28 and its silver bars.  Probed live
# 06-Sep-26: LEFT reached "YOU ARE IN A LOW N/S PASSAGE AT A HOLE IN THE
# FLOOR ... THERE ARE BARS OF SILVER HERE!" with the snake still alive.
#
# The gate is spelled in the TABLE and not in mtkSnakeCheck for LEFT and
# FORWARD because the two shapes are player-visible-identical, and that is
# measured, not assumed: the same probe typed RIGHT (a table `cond SNAKE`
# row) and NORTH (the code bounce) at the same snake and got byte-identical
# replies -- "YOU CAN'T GET BY THE SNAKE." then "YOU'RE IN HALL OF MT
# KING." then the snake's here-text.  A table row costs nothing; a code arm
# costs bank 0 and, for FORWARD, would also need dfdCheckRoom's "not at a
# fissure bank" path to reach the room dispatch, since doMove dispatches
# DIR_FORWARD by direction well before curRoom is tested.
exit NORTH R_HOLE
exit LEFT R_HOLE cond SNAKE msg SNAKE_BLOCKED
exit WEST R_MTKING_WEST cond SNAKE msg SNAKE_BLOCKED
exit FORWARD R_MTKING_WEST cond SNAKE msg SNAKE_BLOCKED
exit SOUTH R_MTKING_SOUTH cond SNAKE msg SNAKE_BLOCKED
exit RIGHT R_MTKING_SOUTH cond SNAKE msg SNAKE_BLOCKED
exit SECRE R_MTKING_CANYON_EW
exit SW R_MTKING_CANYON_EW
exit UP R_MISTHALL
