# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# TASK-SCENERY-NOUNS (S15, 03-Sep-26). The five adven.dat section-7
# objects this port modelled as room state instead of as object rows, so
# four of their nouns did not parse at all and TROLL parsed only for the
# three verbs carrying a bespoke strCmpEq hook. They are ordinary rows
# now, in the same shape the port already uses for every other piece of
# named-but-inert scenery (STEPS, DRAWINGS, STALACTITE, CARPETMOSS,
# MIRROR, VOLCANO, EA1PANEL): take no, invmsg none, heremsg none -- so
# nothing describes them, nothing lists them and nothing can carry them.
# The state each one stands for is untouched; only the noun is new.
#
# Each is a PLAC/FIXD pair in section 7, which makes AT() true in TWO
# rooms. objLoc holds the PLAC room and objPresenceGate's pgSecondLoc
# answers the FIXD one -- the machinery that was already there for
# DRAGON, RUG, STEPS and SHADOWFIG.
#
# objLoc: grate: adven.dat "3 8 9" (PLAC=8 outside the grate,
# objLoc: grate: FIXD=9 below it) -- the second room is in pgSecondLoc.
# objTake: grate -- FIXED(GRATE) is 9, so f4 9010's SPK=25 answers TAKE.
# objInvMsg/objHereMsg: grate -- adven.dat has no section-5 text for it;
# objHereMsg: grate -- the two rooms' own descriptions carry the grate,
# objHereMsg: grate -- and printGrateStatus prints its lock/open state.
object GRATE name voc_grate loc R_GRATE take no invmsg none heremsg none treasure 0

