# msg 50 (TASK-FR27 N11, 05-Sep-26).  adven.dat section 4 gives SESAM,
# OPENS, ABRA, ABRAC, SHAZA and HOCUS the special code 3050, and 2630
# sends a class-4 word to 2010, which speaks MOD(3050,1000) -- msg 50,
# not msg 42.  The header said "msg 42" and every row named
# NOTHING_HAPPENS, which is msg 42's text and belongs to XYZZY/PLUGH
# elsewhere (adven.f4 label 50's "IF(K.EQ.62.OR.K.EQ.65)SPK=42").
# POCUS is not in adven.dat at all -- it is this port's own extra
# spelling of HOCUS POCUS -- and is kept, answering with the family.
verb SESAM voc sesam msgref FR8_MAGIC_WORD_WORN_OUT handler doSpeak
verb OPENS voc opens msgref FR8_MAGIC_WORD_WORN_OUT handler doSpeak
verb ABRA voc abra msgref FR8_MAGIC_WORD_WORN_OUT handler doSpeak
